# charon integration step 39 after 546078ea5d: commit 9b4eec39818095d046fa64a02af3420147e16cf3
# first parent c6b2825aac2708f682b9e8b71ea61dde2eb70ba7
# series charon: patch -p1 in charon/ of the upstream source
#
# charon: --opaque-hard/--opaque-hard-file keep items opaque as #[charon::opaque] does
#
# Partial monomorphization instantiates the generic items that --opaque makes opaque with their
# contents (c6b2825), so that a separately translated chunk can instantiate the items of earlier
# chunks. The native shell of a code base (e.g. primitives that a Lean model replaces) has no
# translation at all, and its generic items' bodies may not be translatable (dyn Any, thread
# locals). --opaque-hard <pattern> and --opaque-hard-file <file> make the matched items (and the
# items nested in them) opaque as if they were annotated with #[charon::opaque]: no body, also
# under --monomorphize-mut, where the generic item stays one signature-only declaration and each
# instance partial monomorphization creates is one signature-only declaration named
# `<generic name>::<shape>`. --exclude still takes precedence; --opaque is unchanged.
#
# The charon binary adds the patterns to --opaque, which the llbc records, and passes them to
# charon-driver in CHARON_OPAQUE_HARD: the CliOpts field is #[serde(skip)] and #[charon::opaque],
# so the serialized options (and charon-ml) are unchanged. UI test monomorphize-mut-opaque-hard;
# help output updated.

